        Based on the commit message and modifications in the patch, you need to analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. 

        Here is the patch content:
        From 2dbd7c5800a71c048e02a6e519cfb243cd994bcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesper Dangaard Brouer <brouer@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Dec 2016 14:17:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] src: udp_flood fix PPS calc and use DEFAULT_COUNT

Fixing bugs introduced in commit 200b8079339c ("flood: move all
options inside a struct").

First fix PPS calculations, which didn't want to provide PPS if
test time was below 1 sec, very strange.  It seemed like a
unintentional changed introduced in the commit.

Second use the DEFAULT_COUNT as the default count value at init.

Fixes: 200b8079339c ("flood: move all options inside a struct")
Signed-off-by: Jesper Dangaard Brouer <brouer@redhat.com>
---
 src/udp_flood.c | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/udp_flood.c b/src/udp_flood.c
index d521f7e..6e02b94 100644
--- a/src/udp_flood.c
+++ b/src/udp_flood.c
@@ -439,7 +439,7 @@ static void time_function(int sockfd, struct flood_params *p,
 	uint64_t tsc_begin,  tsc_end,  tsc_interval;
 	uint64_t time_begin, time_end, time_interval;
 	int cnt_send;
-	double pps=0, ns_per_pkt=0, timesec=0;
+	double pps, ns_per_pkt=0, timesec=0;
 	uint64_t tsc_cycles = 0;

 	time_begin = gettime();
@@ -459,8 +459,7 @@ static void time_function(int sockfd, struct flood_params *p,
 	}

 	/* Stats */
-	if (time_interval / NANOSEC_PER_SEC)
-		pps = cnt_send / ((double)time_interval / NANOSEC_PER_SEC);
+	pps = cnt_send / ((double)time_interval / NANOSEC_PER_SEC);
 	if (cnt_send) {
 		tsc_cycles = tsc_interval / cnt_send;
 		ns_per_pkt = ((double)time_interval / cnt_send);
@@ -473,7 +472,7 @@ static void time_function(int sockfd, struct flood_params *p,
 static void init_params(struct flood_params *params)
 {
 	memset(params, 0, sizeof(struct flood_params));
-	params->count  = 1000000;
+	params->count  = DEFAULT_COUNT;
 	params->batch = 32;
 	params->msg_sz = 18; /* 18 +14(eth)+8(UDP)+20(IP)+4(Eth-CRC) = 64 bytes */
 	params->pmtu = -1;
-- 
2.25.1



        Provide a response strictly in the following format:
        Root cause:<Root cause>

    You are a programming expert.
    You will be given the root cause of a bug and  the corresponding patch.
    You need to extract the code statements that lead to the bug from  the patch, based on the root cause.


    Provide a response strictly in the following format:
    Code statements:
    <text1>
    <text2>
    <text3>
    <text4>
    ...
    <textN>

Root cause:
The root cause of the bug was due to an unintended change in the calculation of packets per second (PPS) during the refactoring in commit 200b8079339c, which incorrectly disabled PPS calculation when the test time was less than 1 second. Additionally, the initial value for the `count` parameter was hardcoded as 1,000,000 instead of using the defined `DEFAULT_COUNT`, which could lead to inconsistent behavior in the initialization of flood parameters.
